[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one parser bug, one fix queued. Its reports say
something else. They hold three problems, and the queued fix closes only one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
The fix queued for #4471 changes the shared parser. It does not change the booking-v3 date hint,
and it does not touch the one-day moves. Those reports stay broken after the fix ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

The table counts the desk's way: one row per report id, since the export repeats some reports.
The one-day moves stay counted under `parser`, where they are filed, and get their own row
under it. Each problem has its own ticket.

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** Every tenant on file writes the
day first, so a date like 4 July comes out as 7 April. It reaches people through the app, by
mail and through booking-v2 forms. This is the bug #4471 names, and the queued fix is for it.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form tells day-first people to type month first.** Its date field
prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under it. People type what the hint says, and the form then reads the date
the tenant's way, day first. The month flips again, for a different reason. Only form reports
from tenants on booking-v3 have this problem. The parser fix leaves this hint as it is.

**`one-day-move`: the date moves by one day, not by months.** These reports describe a
Tuesday that shows as Monday, a meeting that two clients in different time zones got on two
different days, and an invite that arrived before its booking. Day and month are not swapped.
This looks like a time zone shift, not a parse. The desk read these reports as one-day moves
(desk notes), but they were filed under `parser` by tenant, so they are hidden inside its count.

## Why one ticket hid three

- The desk merges on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) and
  never reads a body. A subject like "Wrong date again" says nothing about the cause: all three
  problems arrive under the same subjects, and the [triage explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) shows
  same-subject pairs with different causes.
- Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser. The tag is a guess and often disagrees with
  the cause: see the "tagged as" column.
- The cause table on #4471 shows `hint` as "not this ticket — no ticket of its own". That was
  true. It has one now.

## What the desk does next

- Keep #4471 for `parser`. Do not close the other two when its fix ships.
- When a merged ticket passes a few dozen reports, read a sample of bodies before calling it known.

